  "body": "### Summary\n`TopicFlagFlow.addFavorite` (LOT-051, #77, merged as d1eed2f) treats HFR's \"Favori positionné avec succès\" page as success. The 2026-10-28 captures show that a logged-out addflag (P03q) gets a page **byte-identical** to the logged-in success (P03a). With an expired session the app would therefore show a favourite as added when nothing changed.\n\nScope\n- Confirm addflag differently: the session must be valid before sending (LOT-044 health), and/or verify afterwards (the topic page or the favourites list shows the favourite). Pick one, document it, and test it on P03q vs P03a.\n- delflag never refuses (a repeated delflag gives the same success, P03k vs P03j): document that removeFlag's success means \"the flag is absent\".\n- manageaction: the sentence depends on the request body (\"Favoris supprimés…\" for the browser body, \"Drapeaux effacés…\" for the legacy body). Accept both as this write's confirmation, or send the browser-shaped body. Record which choice, citing the captures.\n- Move LOT-051's tests and spec \"Pending capture\" section onto the new captures P03g–P03q.\n\nBlocked by: the capture PR \"capture: flag and favourite write answers (LOT-051 inputs)\" (Refs #304, #305).\n\nAcceptance criteria\n- A test on P03q shows that addFavorite never returns success without a confirmed session.\n- Each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n",
